igher term and completed a committed command before an old leader VerifyLeader invocation, that old invocation must not return success solely from earlier-term positive replies produced before the new election.',source_ids=q['source_ids'],scope=dict(description='One real cluster history with later leadership and successful Apply completed before old verification invocation. Held old-term replies may be delivered after registration; other old-leader traffic is finitely delayed or disconnected. Public verification success is the primary endpoint; stale FSM contents are optional additional observations.',assumptions=['Fixed voter membership; all successful reply producers are legitimate voters.','Actual bootstrap/elections/Apply generate the prefix; no direct term/role/commit mutation.','The higher-term leader Apply.Error completion must causally precede old VerifyLeader call.','Lease and negative-response workers remain running. Controlled delays and partitions are non-Byzantine and finite; any suppressed path is explicitly described.'],excluded=['General correctness or log-safety violation.','Configuration changes and crash recovery.','Liveness claim from pending verification or cutoff.']),pending=['Construct and execute a same-history transition and correlated public completion comparison.'],grounding=dict(source_ids=['s-heartbeat','s-replication','s-match-notify','s-leader-loop','s-verify-vote','s-vote','s-campaign','s-transfer'],expectation_ids=['s-verify-api','s-verify-documentation'],binding_ids=[b['id'] for b in binds],derivation='VerifyLeader is documented to ensure the peer is still leader and may prevent returning stale FSM data. A distinct higher-term leader with a completed committed command before invocation rules out interpreting the old node as authoritative at any point after admission. Earlier replies cannot establish the promised current authority merely by being delivered to a newly registered future. This derives a necessary rejection condition, not a requirement of successful verification on the new leader or a general linearizable-read specification.',applicability='Ordinary public VerifyLeader under fixed all-voter membership and legal delay/partition faults. The check must establish actual higher-term election and successful command completion independently of old verification output.',unresolved=q['unknowns'],conflicts=[],alternatives=['If lease expires or a higher-term/negative reply reaches the old node first, it may correctly fail verification; such outcomes must remain visible.','An in-flight success from before admission alone proves no violation unless later authority was independently established before invocation.']))\ns=dict(action='obligation',question=q,obligation=o,bindings=binds,rationale='Investigate a distinct authority-context freshness proposition on the shared notification lifecycle. The completed nonvoter eligibility proposition remains closed and unchanged. A later real election and committed write would discriminate delayed valid-at-production support from current authority.',sources=[dict(id='s-pipeline-send-fresh',file='replication.go',start_line=512,end_line=531,kind='code_observation'),dict(id='s-net-response-errors',file='net_transport.go',start_line=742,end_line=789,kind='code_observation'),dict(id='s-response-layout',file='commands.go',start_line=52,end_line=74,kind='code_observation')],feedback=dict(ref_ids=['s-pipeline-send-fresh','s-net-response-errors','s-response-layout','s-rpc','s-heartbeat','s-leader-loop','s-verify-api'],answered='Pipeline reading confirms fresh response allocation and receiver success-after-processing, plus connection release on decoding failure. Missing Error() remains an interface discrepancy, but a partially decoded positive reply does not alone establish support for an unstored entry. Preserve that lead with a precise gap: show a legal producer/error history that changes support meaning, rather than treating the absent check as consensus corruption.',remaining=['Pipeline API misuse remains source-grounded but no stronger consumer consequence is established.','The new authority-freshness question needs same-execution response production, transition, committed write, verification admission and public result.'],understanding='updated',rationale='Compare remaining directions: pipeline error safety requires a producer that undermines the successful field; heartbeat contact liveness lacks a sourced deadline; delayed verification replies have a direct public authority promise and a feasible real-cluster discriminator. Existing notification, campaign and application map objects suffice for this independent question. Preserve the completed eligibility witness and investigate freshness without changing its obligation.'))\njson.dump(s,open('freshness-obligation.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,subprocess\nr=json.load(open('../research.json'));p=subprocess.run(r['validation']['command']+['freshness-obligation.json'],capture_output=True,text=True);print(p.stdout)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
